:""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-13.png","sigTs":1771257180000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-16","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-16","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-00.jpg","ts":1771281180000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-01.jpg","ts":1771281180000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-02.jpg","ts":1771281180000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-03.jpg","ts":1771281720000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-04.jpg","ts":1771289160000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-05.jpg","ts":1771289160000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-06.jpg","ts":1771289220000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-07.jpg","ts":1771289220000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-08.jpg","ts":1771289220000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-09.jpg","ts":1771289340000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-10.jpg","ts":1771290420000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-11.jpg","ts":1771290420000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-12.jpg","ts":1771290420000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-16-13.jpg","ts":1771290480000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":49,"c":"Clear","w":"16","p":".0","h":"70"},{"t":64,"c":"Clear","w":"14","p":".0","h":"38"},{"t":74,"c":"Clear","w":"8","p":".0","h":"25"}],"notes":"Griffith set hollow core on the west side of the DVO. MJE stripped forms from walls 31 and 41, but the work is still not completed. Dirt crews continued working on housing pads. Bennet continued backfilling HDPE between the DVO and the boiler and gas mixing room. Lakeside was off. Midwest cleaned up the concrete on the walls that were poured on Friday and began preparing to install the west side back wall. QDC continued running wire from the transformers to the main electrical room. The DVO crew arrived and began air testing Cell 5. Photos were added to the report, and another picture of the gauges will be taken after the 12-hour testing period.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-16.png","sigTs":1771344240000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-17","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-17","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-00.jpg","ts":1771343940000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-01.jpg","ts":1771343940000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-02.jpg","ts":1771343940000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-03.jpg","ts":1771352580000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-04.jpg","ts":1771367580000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-05.jpg","ts":1771375320000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-06.jpg","ts":1771375500000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-07.jpg","ts":1771375500000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-08.jpg","ts":1771431780000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-09.jpg","ts":1771431780000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-10.jpg","ts":1771431780000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-11.jpg","ts":1771435920000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-12.jpg","ts":1771435920000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-13.jpg","ts":1771435980000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-17-14.jpg","ts":1771435980000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":53,"c":"Clear","w":"13","p":".0","h":"71"},{"t":62,"c":"Clear","w":"17","p":".0","h":"45"},{"t":72,"c":"Partially cloudy","w":"21","p":".0","h":"30"}],"notes":"Griffith was off. MJE removed the remaining forms on walls 31 and 41. The dirt crews worked on housing.\nBennet began preparing and excavating for boring operations. The DVO crew started moving and anchoring racks in place in Digester 4. I will also attach photos of their air testing gauges; two out of the three tests passed. They will need to return to Digester 5 to locate the leaks and conduct a retest. The Midwest crew began installing stainless steel piping on the H2S tanks. The QDC crew continued running wires to cabinets and 480V panels.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-17.png","sigTs":1771438920000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-18","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-18","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-00.jpg","ts":1771435920000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-01.jpg","ts":1771435920000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-02.jpg","ts":1771435980000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-03.jpg","ts":1771452720000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-04.jpg","ts":1771452720000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-05.jpg","ts":1771452960000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-06.jpg","ts":1771453080000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-07.jpg","ts":1771453140000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-08.jpg","ts":1771453860000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-09.jpg","ts":1771461540000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-10.jpg","ts":1771461540000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-11.jpg","ts":1771461540000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-12.jpg","ts":1771461540000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-13.jpg","ts":1771461600000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-18-14.jpg","ts":1771461660000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":35,"c":"Clear","w":"4","p":".0","h":"64"},{"t":59,"c":"Clear","w":"13","p":".0","h":"21"},{"t":64,"c":"Clear","w":"16","p":".0","h":"19"}],"notes":"Griffith was off. MJE filled tie holes and picked up blankets. The dirt crews worked on the housing pads.\nBennet continued backfilling on the east side of DVO and prepped for the road bore. The DVO crew finished anchoring and connecting racks in Cell 4 and also air tested Cell 4; I added pictures of the gauges in the report. The DVO electrician continued installing cable trays on the hollow core. P1 Service came out and staged their equipment in the small electrical room. The QDC crew continued running wires to cabinets and wiring the 480V panels. The Midwest crew continued putting up walls in the middle of the gas mixing room and boiler room and continued installing stainless steel pipes on the H2S tanks.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-18.png","sigTs":1771534680000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-19","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-19","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-00.jpg","ts":1771525320000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-01.jpg","ts":1771533180000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-02.jpg","ts":1771533240000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-03.jpg","ts":1771537260000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-04.jpg","ts":1771537380000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-05.jpg","ts":1771540380000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-06.jpg","ts":1771540380000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-07.jpg","ts":1771542600000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-08.jpg","ts":1771542600000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-09.jpg","ts":1771545480000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-19-10.jpg","ts":1771545480000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":39,"c":"Clear","w":"14","p":".0","h":"56"},{"t":34,"c":"Partially cloudy","w":"23","p":".0","h":"52"},{"t":37,"c":"Clear","w":"19","p":".0","h":"42"}],"notes":"Griffith and P1 Service were off today. MJE finished the tie holes and started forming the exterior curb. The dirt crews completed the housing pads. The Bennet crew bored the sale gas line, fiber line, and return line; I included videos of the work in the report. The Midwest wall crew was off due to high winds, but their second crew installed the ladder on the H2S tanks. QDC ran lights in the main electrical room. The DVO crew left early due to a snowstorm on their way home. The DVO electrician stayed on site and installed the troughs in the main electrical room and disconnects in the boiler room.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-19.png","sigTs":1771610580000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-20","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-20","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-00.jpg","ts":1771626180000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-01.jpg","ts":1771626240000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-02.jpg","ts":1771629300000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-03.jpg","ts":1771630560000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-04.jpg","ts":1771630560000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-05.jpg","ts":1771630560000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-06.jpg","ts":1771630560000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-07.jpg","ts":1771635000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-08.jpg","ts":1771635000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-09.jpg","ts":1771635000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-10.jpg","ts":1771635060000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-11.jpg","ts":1771635060000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-12.jpg","ts":1771635240000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-13.jpg","ts":1771635240000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-14.jpg","ts":1771862760000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-20-15.jpg","ts":1771862760000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":15,"c":"Clear","w":"5","p":".0","h":"83"},{"t":28,"c":"Partially cloudy","w":"6","p":".0","h":"49"},{"t":38,"c":"Clear","w":"10","p":".0","h":"36"}],"notes":"MJE continued forming the exterior wall. Bennet\u2019s crew continued backfilling the HDPE pipes between the DVO structures. QDC continued running wire and installing lights in the main electrical room. Williamson Home Electrician was on site today and began running wire in the office building. Midwest continued placing walls. Griffith began placing hollow core panels; unfortunately, there was a serious accident when one of the hollow core panels failed. Chris, the foreman for Griffith, suffered a broken hand and four fractures to his back. He was transported to the hospital and underwent surgery. As of the latest update on 2/23/26, the surgery went well and he is in good spirits","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-20.png","sigTs":1771863660000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-23","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-23","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-00.jpg","ts":1771953360000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-01.jpg","ts":1771953420000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-02.jpg","ts":1771973400000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-03.jpg","ts":1771973400000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-04.jpg","ts":1771973460000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-05.jpg","ts":1771973460000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-06.jpg","ts":1771973520000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-07.jpg","ts":1771973520000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-23-08.jpg","ts":1771973520000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":20,"c":"Clear","w":"6","p":".0","h":"67"},{"t":40,"c":"Clear","w":"15","p":".0","h":"31"},{"t":50,"c":"Clear","w":"19","p":".0","h":"27"}],"notes":"Griffith was off. MJE consolidated crews, went over safety rules, and organized forms and materials. Dirt crews were off. Bennet added a cleanout to the DVO and continued backfilling the DVO HDPE pipes. Midwest continued adding walls on the west side. QDC crew continued installing lights in the main electrical building.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-23.png","sigTs":1772032200000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-24","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-24","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-24-00.jpg","ts":1771973400000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-24-01.jpg","ts":1772034420000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-24-02.jpg","ts":1772034420000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-24-03.jpg","ts":1772034420000,"cap":""}],"att":[],"wx":[{"t":42,"c":"Clear","w":"14","p":".0","h":"44"},{"t":65,"c":"Clear","w":"9","p":".0","h":"20"},{"t":74,"c":"Clear","w":"6","p":".0","h":"14"}],"notes":"Griffith was off today. MJE continued working and organized forms and materials on site. Dirt crews were off.\nBennet worked on backfilling the east side of the DVO. Lakeside came by to stage their equipment and prepare to continue welding. Midwest continued placing the west side walls everyone left at 11:00pm so we didn\u2019t have much progress on anything.\nWe held our large safety meeting this morning, and it went well. Everyone understands the safety expectations moving forward. I attached a sign-in sheet in the report with all crew members and foremen accounted for.\nAn OSHA representative came out today. We had an opening conference with MJE, Griffith Steel, and Hartman to discuss what happened Friday regarding the accident. He went down into the DVO area, took pictures, and asked questions about how the incident occurred. He will be conducting one-on-one interviews with an MJE employee and a Griffith employee, which I understand will be held over the phone.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-24.png","sigTs":1772034600000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-25","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-25","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-00.jpg","ts":1772054280000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-01.jpg","ts":1772054280000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-02.jpg","ts":1772063040000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-03.jpg","ts":1772063040000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-04.jpg","ts":1772063880000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-05.jpg","ts":1772065380000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-06.jpg","ts":1772065380000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-07.jpg","ts":1772065380000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-08.jpg","ts":1772065440000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-09.jpg","ts":1772065920000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-10.jpg","ts":1772065920000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-11.jpg","ts":1772066220000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-25-12.jpg","ts":1772066220000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":34,"c":"Clear","w":"3","p":".0","h":"81"},{"t":61,"c":"Clear","w":"9","p":".0","h":"31"},{"t":73,"c":"Clear","w":"15","p":".0","h":"23"}],"notes":"Griffith was off. MJE grouted the hollow core seams, poured the hood opening, and poured and grouted openings on the east side of the DVO. The dirt crews were off. Bennet continued backfilling on the east side of the DVO. Williamson continued wiring the office building and installed their lights in the mechanic shops.\nThe Lakeside crew finished the final butt welds and large \ufb02anges, welded stands, and cut in the moisture drops. The QDC crew built a rack for the PVC sleeves, secured the PVC pipes, began running wire for the subpanel, and installed 120V outlets. The crane has still not been serviced; we are waiting on insurance to inspect it, so cleanup inside the DVO cannot begin until the crane has been serviced.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-25.png","sigTs":1772128920000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-26","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-26","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-00.jpg","ts":1771973520000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-01.jpg","ts":1771973520000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-02.jpg","ts":1772146260000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-03.jpg","ts":1772146260000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-04.jpg","ts":1772230200000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-05.jpg","ts":1772238840000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-06.jpg","ts":1772238840000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-07.jpg","ts":1772238840000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-08.jpg","ts":1772238840000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-26-09.jpg","ts":1772238840000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":34,"c":"Clear","w":"8","p":".0","h":"88"},{"t":64,"c":"Clear","w":"13","p":".0","h":"32"},{"t":68,"c":"Clear","w":"17","p":".0","h":"23"}],"notes":"Griffith was off today. MJE finished grouting the openings on the east side of the DVO and cleaned and organized materials. The dirt crews were off. Bennet continued backfilling on the east side of the DVO.\nLakeside Pipe finished the moisture drops and o-lets. QDC continued adding lights in the main building and running wire for the subpanel. P1 Service came out and continued working on the HVAC system in the small electrical room.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-26.png","sigTs":1772466300000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2026-02-27","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2026-02-27","by":"Bryan Ricca","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-00.jpg","ts":1772230200000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-01.jpg","ts":1772230200000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-02.jpg","ts":1772230260000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-03.jpg","ts":1772230260000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-04.jpg","ts":1772238840000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-05.jpg","ts":1772238840000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-06.jpg","ts":1772238840000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-07.jpg","ts":1772467140000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-08.jpg","ts":1772467140000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-09.jpg","ts":1772467140000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-10.jpg","ts":1772467140000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2026-02-27-11.jpg","ts":1772467200000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":38,"c":"Clear","w":"6","p":".0","h":"60"},{"t":73,"c":"Clear","w":"18","p":".0","h":"23"},{"t":75,"c":"Clear","w":"10","p":".0","h":"21"}],"notes":"Griffith was off, and Bennett was also off today. Midwest got all the concrete poured on the west wall.\nLakeside crew was onsite for about half a day and continued welding the moisture traps. QDC anchored the AW cabinets in the main electrical room and continued running wire to the mechanical shop. Williamson continued running lights in the mechanical shop room. MJE finished the cleanouts on the DVO openings.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2026-02-27.png","sigTs":1772467380000,"source":"Raken PDF"}]}